Cross-check vs HYP-2739 published P=7 f (rowdef): they must agree.
   our S_7(3,3) = 428 = 7 * 61  ; HYP-2739 rowdef max should be 44:  rowdef(3,3)=61
   (HYP-2739's 'S=4f' uses S=rowdef and that table maxes at 44 -> matches rowdef.)

   our rowdef (=S/7) table vs HYP-2739 S-table (||a||,||b|| 0..3):
     identical: False

Bernoulli form of the edge parabola g(t)=2t(P-t):
   g(t) = 2t(P-t) = (P^2 - (P-2t)^2)/2.  With ||ab||=t, (P-2t)=|P-2(ab mod P)|.
   And t(P-t)/P^2 = 1/4 - (B_1(t/P))^2 where B_1(x)=x-1/2 ((;)) ... i.e. a
   pure even function of (t/P-1/2), the <-1>-quotient coordinate.  So g is a
   value of the degree-2 Bernoulli/theta on Z/P modulo +-1.  QED-shape.
